  "Question": "What is the value of\n\n\\[(2 \\times 3 \\times 4)\\left(\\frac{1}{2} + \\frac{1}{3} + \\frac{1}{4}\\right)?\\]",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(1\\)",
    "B": "\\(3\\)",
    "C": "\\(9\\)",
    "D": "\\(24\\)",
    "E": "\\(26\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "E",
  "Solution": "The product \\(2\\cdot3\\cdot4=24\\) is divisible by each denominator. Distributing \\(24\\) across the three fractions therefore turns each term into a whole number:\n\\[\n\\begin{aligned}\n24\\left(\\frac12+\\frac13+\\frac14\\right)\n&=\\frac{24}{2}+\\frac{24}{3}+\\frac{24}{4}\\\\\n&=12+8+6=26.\n\\end{aligned}\n\\]\nThe value is \\(26\\), choice \\(\\mathrm{E}\\).",
